+export function mountEntrance(host){let view='oblique',labels=true;host.innerHTML=`<div class="entrance-intro"><p class="eyebrow">A DIFFERENT PART OF KRYPTOS</p><h2>The entrance: granite, compass and lodestone.</h2><p>At the New Headquarters Building’s west entrance, an engraved compass rose and a nearby naturally magnetized rock form part of the installation. They are <strong>separate from the courtyard copper screen</strong>.</p><p class="modelnote">Original illustrative rendering from inspected photographs. Shapes, relief and spacing are approximations. No dimensions, surveyed bearing, line of sight or magnetic field are assigned.</p></div><div class="entrance-tools" role="group" aria-label="Entrance illustration controls"><button type="button" data-entrance-view="oblique" aria-pressed="true">Oblique view</button><button type="button" data-entrance-view="plan" aria-pressed="false">Overhead view</button><label><input id="entrance-labels" type="checkbox" checked> Interpretation labels</label></div><div id="entrance-drawing"></div><p id="entrance-view-status" role="status" class="mono"></p><div class="entrance-notes"><article><h3>Three axes, not one bearing</h3><p>The letters mark the <strong>engraved N axis</strong>. The elongated needle is <strong>fixed carving</strong>, shown at a different local angle. Neither is registered to <strong>true north</strong> here.</p><p>A 2005 attendee account attributes an intended direction toward the lodestone. No exact surveyed bearing is established. A reported approximate bearing is not a measurement; no direction is fitted to the K4 clues.</p></article><article><h3>Where does it belong?</h3><p>The entrance and courtyard are separated by the building. This relationship diagram is <strong>schematic, not survey scale</strong>; it is not a route or sightline.</p><ol class="entrance-relationship" aria-label="Schematic relationship: entrance, building, courtyard"><li>West entrance<br><strong>Rose + lodestone</strong></li><li><strong>New Headquarters Building</strong><br>between installations</li><li>Courtyard<br><strong>Copper screen</strong></li></ol></article></div><details><summary>Visual sources and limits</summary><p>The close-up shows a flat slab, simple circular engraving, letters, a long carved needle and an adjacent irregular rock. The aerial locates the entrance walkway and courtyard on different sides of the building. This drawing copies no source photograph pixels. It is not a traced or calibrated reconstruction. Other entrance granite/copper/Morse-code pieces are omitted.</p><p>The view controls change the illustration only. No magnetic needle animation, magnetic-field calculation or cryptanalytic hypothesis test is performed.</p><ul>${ENTRANCE_SOURCES.map(([title,url])=>`<li><a href="${url}" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">${title}</a></li>`).join('')}</ul></details>`;
+ const drawing=host.querySelector('#entrance-drawing'),status=host.querySelector('#entrance-view-status');function render(){drawing.innerHTML=entranceDrawing(view,labels);status.textContent=(view==='plan'?'Overhead':'Oblique')+' illustration · fixed needle · true north unregistered';for(const button of host.querySelectorAll('[data-entrance-view]'))button.setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(button.dataset.entranceView===view));}
+ for(const button of host.querySelectorAll('[data-entrance-view]'))button.onclick=()=>{view=button.dataset.entranceView;render();};host.querySelector('#entrance-labels').onchange=e=>{labels=e.target.checked;render();};render();return{getState:()=>({view,labels}),reset(){view='oblique';labels=true;host.querySelector('#entrance-labels').checked=true;render();}};
+}
